{
  "sentiment": "positive",
  "review": "It would seem we should acknowledge Scandinavian cinema for more than merely the Dogma 1995 movement as cooked up by the Danish all those years ago. Den Brysomme Mannen, or The Bothersome Man in English, is a surreal and deeply thought through film yet deeply entertaining and rich in content both on and under the surface. As a film alone, it is a scathing comedy on society and attitudes in the post-modern world we live in; a world that judging by The Bothersome Man, the protagonist might have ended up in purgatory. The film's best part is the one that sneaks up on you: the contrast between 'heaven' and 'hell' as briefly shown in the closing five minutes, which suddenly informs you of the reality faced by Andreas and his freethinking, adventurous mind  and look where the thinkers end up.",
