{
  "sentiment": "positive",
  "review": "There is a complete copy now available at the Internet Archive - watch it or download it today! http://www.archive.org/details/The_Mascot_Complete One of the greatest animated shorts ever made. Starewicz is endlessly inventive and his techniques still astound animation fans 70 years later. We may have computer-generated techniques now, but all he had in 1934 was an imagination that wouldn't take 'no' for an answer. Whatever he wanted to see on the screen, he created. And he wanted to see some truly bizarre stuff - every imaginable piece of scrap is called up for service: old shoes, chicken bones, utensils, broken glasses, dolls, monkeys, rats....seems like there was nothing that was off limits. A truly eerie, even unsettling film that should be seen by anyone with even a passing interest in animation. This film must be seen to be believed!",
